(BAS-48 - the three-nested-ifs example, LANGUAGE.md:216-221, verbatim.
 Three periods close the innermost `if`, then the middle one, then the
 outer one, so the last statement runs at the top level even though every
 condition is false.
 Also covers: BAS-47 (periods stack - one period per level to close).
